{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# ML-03 — Frame Your Lane as an ML Task\n","\n","[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/alberttigo24-droid/Albert-Flyrank-assignments/blob/main/work/notebooks/w02_ml_task_framing.ipynb?flush_cache=true)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. My lane as an ML task (type)\n","\n","**Lane 2 — Refresh / Content Opportunity Scoring** is primarily a **ranking/scoring** problem. The practical question is which pages should be reviewed first when review capacity is limited. The output is a priority score and ranked review queue. Ranking fits because the decision is about ordering candidates, and Precision@K matches a workflow where a reviewer can act on only the first K pages. ML is decision support for the human reviewer, not an automatic final content decision."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"metadata":{},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":"Task type: ranking / scoring\nOutput: priority score and ranked review queue\nPrimary success metric: Precision@K\n"}],"source":["task_type = 'ranking / scoring'\noutput = 'priority score and ranked review queue'\nmetric = 'Precision@K'\nprint('Task type:', task_type)\nprint('Output:', output)\nprint('Primary success metric:', metric)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Target or proxy\n","\n","For the starter dataset, the immediate **proxy** is `is_declining_label`, derived from `trend_direction == \"down\"`. It is a current-window proxy, not an ideal future target. For a stronger later version, I would define a future observed outcome, such as decline in a specified future window, using features only from an earlier window. This separation is necessary to avoid leakage. I will not treat the proxy as proof that a refresh will work."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"metadata":{},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":"Proxy positive rate: 54.2%\n"}],"source":["import pandas as pd\n","df = pd.read_csv('../../data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv')\n","df['is_declining_proxy'] = df['trend_direction'].eq('down')\n","print('Proxy positive rate: {:.1f}%'.format(df['is_declining_proxy'].mean() * 100))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Success metric\n","\n","My primary metric is **Precision@K**, with K chosen to match realistic review capacity (for example, 20 or 50 pages). It asks how many of the first K pages in the ranking are positive under the chosen target/proxy. This is better aligned with the decision than generic accuracy because the team will not act on every page. I will compare the learned ranking with a transparent fixed-rule baseline before claiming that ML adds value."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"metadata":{},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":"Decision-aligned evaluation: Precision@50\n"}],"source":["K = 50\nprint(f'Decision-aligned evaluation: Precision@{K}')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. The unit of analysis, as a real dataframe\n","\n","**One row = one pseudonymized content page.** The starter dataset has 30,000 rows and `content_id` is unique in this slice. `client_id` is useful for grouping or holdout checks, but it is not a model feature. The dataframe below shows the page-level unit and observable signals that could be available at decision time."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"metadata":{},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":"Shape: (30000, 7)\nUnique content pages: 30000\nOne row = one content page\n"},{"data":{"text/plain":["          content_id        client_id  impressions_90d  clicks_90d  sessions_90d  content_age_days trend_direction\ncontent_304f48230142 client_f369cb89fc             3803          29            17               187            down\ncontent_a1fb4e703a9e client_4e07408562            15320           7             9               445            down\ncontent_9aa793d4d895 client_7f2253d7e2            12581          11            11               141            down\ncontent_331d6c4de07b client_19581e27de            11751          58            78               463          stable\ncontent_d99b7a2d90ca client_3fdba35f04            19140          24           145               263            down\ncontent_d4084a4bc775 client_f369cb89fc             3970           1            5               147            down\ncontent_9a34b442b552 client_8722616204               20           0            1                90            down\ncontent_a63219c6e95a client_19581e27de             1724           1           28               445          stable"]}},"metadata":{}}],"source":["lane_df = df[['content_id','client_id','impressions_90d','clicks_90d','sessions_90d','content_age_days','trend_direction']].copy()\n","print('Shape:', lane_df.shape)\n","print('Unique content pages:', lane_df['content_id'].nunique())\n","print('One row = one content page')\n","display(lane_df.head(8))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Why ML beats a fixed rule here\n","\n","A fixed rule is an important baseline, but useful signals can interact in ways that are difficult to express with a few thresholds. A page can have high impressions but weak CTR, be old but still valuable, show movement with different engagement evidence, or have several moderate signals that become important together.\n","\n","I do **not** assume ML is better. ML earns its place only if it reliably improves the ranking over a transparent rule under honest validation. I will compare a learned ranking with a simple baseline using Precision@K, while keeping reason codes and human review."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"metadata":{},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":"Baseline: transparent rule-based ranking\nML candidate: learned ranking model\nRequirement: higher Precision@K under leakage-safe validation\n"}],"source":["print('Baseline: transparent rule-based ranking')\n","print('ML candidate: learned ranking model')\n","print('Requirement: higher Precision@K under leakage-safe validation')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Self-check\n","\n","- [x] Task type: ranking/scoring\n","- [x] Target/proxy named and limitation explained\n","- [x] Success metric: Precision@K\n","- [x] Real dataframe shown; one row = one content page\n","- [x] Output supports a real content action through a prioritized human review queue\n","- [x] ML is not assumed to be better; it must beat a transparent baseline\n","- [x] No client names, URLs, private queries, or raw content text are used\n","- [x] Claims are careful: observed, directional, decision-support"]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}